    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: Backpackers Rainy-Day Planning</h1>
    <p>Rain is part of Hanoi's year, and a backpacker's month of riding will meet it. The trip that plans for wet days, gear packed, technique adjusted, schedules flexed, keeps the rain a weather event instead of a trip event, and this page is that plan: what to carry, how a loaded rental bike behaves in the wet, when to ride and when a cafe and a banh mi is the better decision, all written cautiously, with no live forecasts and no promises about any particular day's sky.</p>
    <p>The page belongs to the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> cluster, written for backpackers. The verified fleet prices are on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, the general question bank is on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page, and the city-wide wet-riding techniques are covered in the <a href="/motorbike-guides/riding-a-motorbike-in-hanoi-rainy-season/">rainy season riding guide</a>, with this page adding the long-trip, loaded-bike layer on top.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">Why wet days are a planning problem</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">The rain kit: what a month carries</li>
        <li><a href="#sec-3">How a loaded bike changes in the wet</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-4">Riding technique for the wet hours</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-5">The wait-or-ride decision</a></li>
